--- body ---
## Context

Observed on 2026-11-13 in climate-finance-het, while landing a stack of three
merge requests (#2154 <- #2160 <- #2166, each based on the previous one's
head branch). That repository has GitHub's `delete_branch_on_merge` on.

- #2154 merged; GitHub deleted its head branch `t2063-round-three-yield`,
  which was the base of #2160. The request was retargeted to `main`.
- The review of #2160 (`rv-20261112-pr-2160-6923`) held requests whose
  `base_ref` was `origin/t2063-round-three-yield`. Once the tracking ref was
  pruned, `review_notes.py` answered `cannot resolve
  origin/t2063-round-three-yield` to `gate`, `verdict` and the answer write
  of `gaze_close.py`.
- Cost: one verify-gate run of 20 minutes ended ESCALATE with nothing
  recorded, although every check had passed; one gaze run of 5 minutes ended
  the same way. A plain relaunch of gaze hit the same wall, because
  `gaze_setup.py` (`reviewed_request`) reuses the latest request on the
  reviewed head, whatever its base.
- Where the binding is read: `review_notes.py` `_append` (the request's
  `base_ref`), `coverage` and `gate_state` (the latest answer's `base_ref`).
- What unblocked it, by hand: `review_notes.py request --review <id>
  --branch <head branch> --base-ref origin/main`, then gaze, then the gate.
  Merge base and range patch-id were unchanged by the retarget.

The same happens to any request whose base branch disappears or whose forge
base changes after its review opened; a stack on an auto-deleting forge
meets it at every level but the top one landed last.

## Scope

The review path (gaze setup and close, the gate's admission and verdict
write) when the forge base of a request differs from the base its latest
request names, or when that base ref no longer resolves. How to handle it is
the implementer's choice: rebind by a new request on the same head, refuse
early with the unblocking command, or resolve the binding from the recorded
base OID instead of the ref name.

Out of scope: the merge recipe's handling of stacks in general.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] A review whose latest request names a base ref that no longer
      resolves, on a request since retargeted to `main`: gaze records its
      answer and verify-gate records its verdict without a hand-written
      request, or both refuse before doing any work and print the command
      that unblocks them.
- [ ] A test reproduces the 2026-11-13 case: a request on a head, its base
      ref deleted, the forge base moved to `main`, same merge base.
- [ ] `skills/merge/SKILL.md` says what to do with a stacked request whose
      base merged, or says nothing is needed.
- [ ] `make check` passes.
